  "summary": "Say what you have and don't have with عِنْدِي, لِي and مَعِي.",
  "intro": "Arabic has no verb 'to have'. It says 'at me there is': عِنْدِي سَيَّارَة (I have a car). لِي (for me) is used for family and for things that belong to you, and مَعِي (with me) for what you have on you right now. To say you don't have something, put لَيْسَ in front: لَيْسَ عِنْدِي تِلْفَاز (I don't have a television).",
